  "name": "map-wayfind",
  "description": "Decision-frontier wayfinding: build and work a durable map of open design decisions BEFORE planning, for large or foggy efforts where /map-plan would force premature decomposition. Use when a task is too big or too vague to decompose — many unknowns, tangled decisions, or \"I'm not even sure what to build yet\" — and you want to resolve the key decisions one at a time (research, prototype, grilling, task tickets) behind a claim-before-work frontier, with a \"fog of war\" for questions you cannot yet state sharply. Produces a handoff that /map-plan consumes. Modes are explicit: chart (start a map), work (resolve one ticket), handoff (finish). Do NOT use when scope is already clear enough to specify — go straight to /map-plan; do NOT use to implement code or to decompose an already-specifiable change.",
